st":72.5,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.015154843300903763,"_gp_fcf_yield":false,"_score_fcf_yield":0.0,"_gate_int_coverage":8.051923076923076,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":37.1,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-0.1473194654582585,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":92.2,"_gate_accruals":-0.043124629281867694,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":39.4,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.19643815264415587,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":58.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.02677227909634186,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.022708824005555697,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.6440891777097277,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.045952484299542566,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":32.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.05733963076157193,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":14.2,"_gate_pool_share":-0.09263118565574469,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":2.9,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.26003145607859457,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.016958674453692486,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":33.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.07132504256808282,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":71.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.043842314672464966,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":59.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.00819506158685901,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":60.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004480917178907565,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.031519998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":21.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"AdvanSix Inc., integrated chemistry company, engages in the manufacture and sale of polymer resins in the United States and internationally. The company offers Nylon 6, a polymer resin, which is a synthetic material used to produce fibers, filaments, engineered plastics, and films. It also provides caprolactam to manufacture polymer resins; ammonium sulfate fertilizers to distributors, farm cooperatives, and retailers; and acetone that are used in the production of adhesives, paints, coatings, solvents, herbicides, and resins. In addition, the company offers intermediate chemicals, including phenol, alpha-methylstyrene, cyclohexanone, oximes, cyclohexanol, and alkyl and specialty amines; and cyclohexanol, sulfuric acid, ammonia, and carbon dioxide, as well as automotive components, water treatment, and pharmaceutical intermediates. It offers its products under the Aegis, Sulf-N, Nadone, Naxol, and EZ-Blox under brand names. The company sells its products directly and through distributors. AdvanSix Inc. was incorporated in 2016 and is headquartered in Parsippany, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Erin N. Kane | CEO, President & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["AdvanSix Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $423M market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $6M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 8.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio of 178% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AdvanSix (ASIX) and Its Rivals Head-To-Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/advansix-asix-and-its-rivals-head-to-head-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794309345.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.85,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in ASIX Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_ASIX_Response_110926111002_1794283802.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794283802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Analyst Estimates: Here's What Brokers Think Of AdvanSix Inc. (NYSE:ASIX) After Its Third-Quarter Report","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-asix/advansix/news/analyst-estimates-heres-what-brokers-think-of-advansix-inc-n","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794146296.136,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"AdvanSix $ASIX Shares Purchased by CenterBook Partners LP","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/advansix-asix-shares-purchased-by-centerbook-partners-lp.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794129190.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AdvanSix declares $0.16 dividend (NYSE:ASIX)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666989-advansix-declares-0_16-dividend","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793900762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"What AdvanSix (ASIX) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","li